  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results achieved</narrative>
    <narrative xml:lang="SV">Uppn&#xe5;dda resultat</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some of the narrative reports that has been assessed includes Burkina Faso, DRC, Nigeria, Sudan, South Sudan, CAR, Yemen, Venezuela, Chad, Cameroon, Ethiopia, Mocambique. 

Some of the key results from 2021 includes:

- In Ethiopia, UNICEF reached approximately 200 000 under the child protection component and GBV through MHPSS services, dignity kits, education opportunities, family reunification and risk mitigation as well as awareness raising. 

- In Mocambique, 1.1 million children under the age of 15 were vaccinated against measles, 320 000 children and women gained access to primary health care and 261 000 beneficiaries were provided with safe access to clean water. 

- In Nigeria, almost 500 000 children received treatment for servere accute malnutrition, personal hygien and access to clean water were provided to 1.6 million beneficiaries and 3 000 children formerly associated with armed groups were reunited with their families. 

- In Yemen, UNICEF provided over 8.8 million people, including 5.3 million children with access to clean water, 800 000 children were vaccinated against measles and almost 8 million went through screening for accute malnutrition. 

In conclusion, the narrative reports are in general of good quality and descriptive but more output and activity oriented and sometimes lacks analysis on impact level,  however, the reports meets Sidas standard requirements. When it comes to follow-up, some of these points will be raised at country level or addressed during the 2022 annual meeting depending on the level of the comment while some will be responded to through e-mail exchange and can be found archived in Dox.</narrative>
   </description>
